# `mid` declares only @test/p1, but the code it compiles names @test/p2's
# `Token` — as `Api`'s return type, and as the ancestor of its own class. Only
# direct dependencies used to reach the compiler, so `Token` had no declaration
# to reconstruct from and the divergent lowering surfaced at link time as
# `imported global type mismatch` / `imported function signature mismatch`.
#
# The consumer has to be a library package: the fixture harness hands the root
# script every declaration in the manifest regardless of its `deps`.
# name          dir    deps                            root
@test/p2        lib2   -
@test/p1        lib1   @test/p2
@test/p3        mid    @test/p1
main            app    @test/p1,@test/p2,@test/p3      root
